Sample size calculation for two independent mean situation
The formula to calculate sample size are taken from the Book of Bernard[(rosner2011?). The formula to caculate sample size in two groups are not equal (r&gt;1) is as follows:
\[n1=\frac{(\sigma_1^2+\frac{\sigma_2^2}{r})(Z_{\alpha/2}+Z_\beta)^2* \sigma}{(u_1-u_2)}
\]
\[n2=\frac{(r*\sigma_1^2+\sigma_2^2)*(Z_{\alpha/2}+Z_\beta)^2}{(u_1-u_2)^2}
\]
The formula to caculate sample size in two groups are equal (r=1) is as follows:
\[n=\frac{(\sigma_1^2+\sigma_2^2)*(Z_{\alpha/2}+Z_\beta)^2}{(u_1-u_2)^2}
\]
The function to calculate sample size for the given condition is as follows:

sscal_twoimean&lt;-function(u1, u2,sd1=NA, sd2=NA, sided.test=c("one.sided", "two.sided"), conf.int=0.95, power=0.80, nratio=1){



  alpha=1-conf.int
  if(sided.test=="two.sided"){
  Za=qnorm(p=1-alpha/2, mean=0, sd=1)
  } else{Za=qnorm(p=1-alpha, mean=0, sd=1)}

  beta=1-power
  Zb=qnorm(p=1-beta, mean=0, sd=1)

  n= (sd1^2+sd2^2)*(Za+Zb)^2/(u1-u2)^2

 n2= (sd1^2+sd2^2/nratio)*(Za+Zb)^2/(u1-u2)^2
  n1= (nratio*sd1^2+sd2^2)*(Za+Zb)^2/(u1-u2)^2
  if(nratio==1){
  cat("Sample size required \n group1: ", ceiling(n), "\n", "group2:", ceiling(n), "\n\n")
  } else{
    cat("Sample size required \n group1: ", ceiling(n1), "\n", "group2:", ceiling(n2), "\n\n")
  }
}

Example: How many non-OC users and OC users are required in a study to compare mean between them. The anticipated mean for group 1 is 132.86 (SD=15.34) and for group 2 is 127.44 (SD=18.23), power of 80% and 95% confidence level. Assume that you chose ratio of sample size is 1:1, 2:1 and 1:3.
(This example is taken from (rosner2011?).)
Solution:
u1=132.86; u2=15.34 ; sd1=15.34; sd2=18.23, nratio=1:1, 2:1 or 3:1
power=80%
Confidence level= 95%

# when nratio=1:1
sscal_twoimean(u1=132.86, u2=127.44, sd1=15.34, sd2=18.23,sided.test = "two.sided", power = 0.8,conf.int = 0.95,nratio =1  )

#&gt; Sample size required 
#&gt;  group1:  152 
#&gt;  group2: 152

# when nratio=2:1
sscal_twoimean(u1=132.86, u2=127.44, sd1=15.34, sd2=18.23,sided.test = "two.sided", power = 0.8,conf.int = 0.95,nratio =2  )

#&gt; Sample size required 
#&gt;  group1:  215 
#&gt;  group2: 108

# when nratio=1:3
sscal_twoimean(u1=132.86, u2=127.44, sd1=15.34, sd2=18.23,sided.test = "two.sided", power = 0.8,conf.int = 0.95,nratio =0.3333)

#&gt; Sample size required 
#&gt;  group1:  110 
#&gt;  group2: 330


Sample size for estimating minimum detectable odds ratio
 

sscal_odds_precision_based&lt;-function(P1, P2=NA,OR=NA, rel.error, conf.int=0.95, power=0.80){
  if(OR&gt;=1){
  if(is.na(P2)){
  P2=P1/(OR*(1-P1)+P1)}
  else{
    P2=P2
  }
  }else {
    if(is.na(P1)){
  "must enter value of P1"}
  else{
    OR=1/OR
  }

  }



  alpha=1-conf.int

  Za=qnorm(p=1-alpha/2, mean=0, sd=1)

  n=Za^2*((1/(P1*(1-P1))+ 1/(P2*(1-P2))))/(log(1-rel.error))^2

  cat("Sample size required \n n: ", ceiling(n))
}

# Calculation
sscal_odds_precision_based(P1 =0.3, P2 = NA, OR=2, rel.error = 0.25,conf.int = 0.95 )

#&gt; Sample size required 
#&gt;  n:  541
